wasm jit: vtype call args keep their source variable through alias analysis (gex)

A by-address vtype argument has no OUTARG copy: the emitter copies straight out of the source
variable's addr slot, so mono_wasm_emit_call marks that variable INDIRECT. Its only use is in
call->out_ireg_args, never an sreg. recompute_aliased_variables clears INDIRECT on every variable
and restores it only for OP_LDADDR targets, so the variable lost it; handle_global_vregs then saw
it in a single bblock, converted it to a local vreg, and mono_local_deadce deleted its def when the
call sat in a later bblock (an inlined Span->ReadOnlySpan conversion feeding Decoder.GetChars).
The emitter found the arg with no def and no addr slot and bailed ("call arg ld: by-addr vtype
source has no addr slot"). Alias analysis now restores INDIRECT for STACK_VTYPE out_ireg_args
variables under COMPILE_WASM, and emit_call promotes a plain vtype vreg to a variable the same way
handle_global_vregs would. The "call arg ld" bail now names its specific reason.
BinaryReader.ReadString, Number.NumberToString<char>, ResourceManager..ctor and
ResourceManager.IsDefaultType now compile. Test: T.Localloc's BinaryReader round trip
(ReadString) and the existing number-formatting lines.

diff --git a/src/mono/mono/mini/alias-analysis.c b/src/mono/mono/mini/alias-analysis.c
index abbdedb43..f04556fec 100644
--- a/src/mono/mono/mini/alias-analysis.c
+++ b/src/mono/mono/mini/alias-analysis.c
@@ -355,6 +355,23 @@ recompute_aliased_variables (MonoCompile *cfg, int *restored_vars)
 				}
 				var->flags |= MONO_INST_INDIRECT;
 			}
+#ifdef TARGET_WASM
+			/* The wasm JIT passes vtype call args by address straight out of the source variable
+			 * (mono_wasm_emit_call marks it INDIRECT; there is no OUTARG copy). That use is only
+			 * visible through out_ireg_args, never as an sreg, so without this the variable loses
+			 * INDIRECT here, handle_global_vregs converts it to a bblock-local vreg, and
+			 * mono_local_deadce deletes its def when the call sits in a later bblock. */
+			else if (COMPILE_WASM (cfg) && MONO_IS_CALL (ins)) {
+				MonoCallInst *call = (MonoCallInst*)ins;
+				for (GSList *l = call->out_ireg_args; l; l = l->next) {
+					MonoInst *var = get_vreg_to_inst (cfg, (guint32)(gssize)l->data & 0xffffff);
+					if (var && (var->type == STACK_VTYPE) && !(var->flags & MONO_INST_INDIRECT)) {
+						++adds;
+						var->flags |= MONO_INST_INDIRECT;
+					}
+				}
+			}
+#endif
 		}
 	}
 	*restored_vars = adds;
